== Changelog ==

### 2.0.7
* Increased compatibility with various WordPress menus

### 2.0.6
* Fixed a bug where checkboxes were not shown

### 2.0.5
* Fixed a bug where Jquery was not loaded

### 2.0.4
* Removed debug messages

### 2.0.3

* Replaced all $ references with jQuery. to ensure compatibility with WordPress standards
* Resolved potential conflicts caused by the use of $ shorthand in JavaScript

### 2.0.2 
* Ensured only one submenu can be opened at a time, improving navigation clarity
* Closed submenus automatically when switching to a different menu item
* Enhanced user experience by preventing overlapping or multiple open submenus
* Retained smooth scrolling and interaction for nested menu structures

### 2.0.1
* Fixed scrollbar behavior for mobile devices
* Improved touch interaction for scrolling within the offcanvas menu
* Enhanced mobile usability for menus with a large number of items

### 2.0.0
* Complete code overhaul for better performance
* Removal of all external dependencies
* Optimized CSS structure following best practices
* Unified menu arrow design
* Improved customizer integration
* Reduced file size
* Faster loading times
* Simplified scrollbar implementation

### 1.4.3
* Removed external dependencies for better performance and compatibility
* Simplified scrollbar implementation
* Improved CSS generation

### 1.4.2
* Update Readme

### 1.2.3
The dropdown arrow now covers the whole menu item. Also a little padding has been added to submenu items.

### 1.2.2
The Customizer-Setting "always active" is now disabled by default. So if you now install the Plugin with any customizations, you will see the default MainMenu unless you set "always" active" to true.

